    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a score of 82.99, **Corbin Carroll** leverages a favorable matchup against King to maximize our 5x5 potential; his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in this scarcest of categories, and his leadoff spot allows him to maximize high-probability stolen base opportunities against a pitcher who struggles to neutralize the run game. **Brice Turang** (73.39) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) also highlight our core, with **Brice Turang** specifically benefiting from a plus-matchup against Chandler and a slow delivery profile that significantly increases our chances of swiping a bag. **Isaac Paredes** continues to be a high-floor play, finding an advantageous spot against a pitcher in Bieber with a ballooning 5.48 xERA.\n\nWhile **Mickey Moniak** holds a starting spot, he remains our most volatile option at 49.81. His high-park-factor boost of +14% is largely negated by a difficult platoon disadvantage and a lackluster opponent xERA, making him a marginal start compared to our high-upside options. **Jose Caballero** also faces a tough road; despite his utility, his score of 54.15 was hampered by a -13% platoon hit and a suboptimal #8 spot in the lineup. Our most interesting bench decision involved weighing **Mickey Moniak** against potential depth pieces like **Zach McKinstry** or **Cole Young**; ultimately, **Mickey Moniak** retained the start solely due to the park-factor tailwind in his specific venue. We are closely monitoring **Seiya Suzuki**, whose score of 66.01 is contingent on his presumed #2 spot in the lineup; should that shift lower, his value\u2014and the efficiency of our lineup\u2014will fluctuate accordingly.",
